WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.850
Washington, 2026.

2
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:07.330
Federal debt held by the
public: 101 per cent of GDP.

3
00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:15.050
The CBO projects 120 per cent by
2036, above its 1946 high of 106.

4
00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:21.630
In the EU, Italy's debt went
from 116.1 to 134.3 per cent,

5
00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:24.690
2009 to 2024.

6
00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:30.930
NASA's Inspector General puts one SLS
and Orion launch at 4.1 billion dollars.

7
00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:36.050
So can the USA and the EU afford
to stay on top until 2050?

8
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:39.430
In this mission, you'll weigh debt, jobs,

9
00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:42.070
industry, and what armies and space cost.

10
00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:46.790
Then you'll judge how the world
might look in 2030 and 2050.

11
00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:52.110
Your mission: evaluate whether the USA
and the EU can afford to stay on top until

12
00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:53.160
2050.
